<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

	<!--
		Alpha Crafts vs Vanilla Cooking Expanded, where both ship the same thing.
		  - Mayonnaise: VCE's mayo and its recipe are cherry-picked; Alpha Crafts' mayonnaise and infused mayonnaise (and,
		    with VPE More Plants, black garlic mayonnaise) join VCE's condiment category, show VCE-style condiment effects,
		    and give VCE's consumed-mayo effect (plain) or their own stronger variants (Defs/ThoughtDefs.xml). The effect
		    descriptions are in Languages/English/Keyed/AlphaCrafts.xml.
		  - Deep frier: VCE's deep frier burns Alpha Crafts oil instead of chemfuel (10 per day instead of 160) and costs 40
		    instead of 75 of its first cost item.
		This folder only loads when Alpha Crafts is active (see loadFolders.xml); each part is gated on VCE, the black
		mayo part also on VPE More Plants.
		Verified against the current 1.6 releases: every target hits, none of the mayos already has a condiment category,
		condiment extension or ingredient thought (Alpha Crafts' own VCE patch covers 13 other condiments but skips them),
		and no installed mod touches the deep frier's fuel or cost. Fishing Treasures lists VCE_Mayo in its fishing loot
		and Progression: Kitchen retunes VCE_Mayo's description and research; both become moot once it is cherry-picked.
		Split by category into the MMMM Convergence sub-mods: this copy holds only the Buildings ops (buildings, furniture, floors, recipes and production).
	-->

	<Operation Class="PatchOperationSequence">
		<operations>
			<li Class="PatchOperationSequence" MayRequire="VanillaExpanded.VCookE">
				<operations>
					<li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
						<xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="VCE_DeepFrier"]/comps/li[@Class="CompProperties_Refuelable"]/fuelConsumptionRate</xpath>
						<value>
							<fuelConsumptionRate>10.0</fuelConsumptionRate>
						</value>
					</li>
					<li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
						<xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="VCE_DeepFrier"]/comps/li[@Class="CompProperties_Refuelable"]/fuelFilter/thingDefs</xpath>
						<value>
							<thingDefs>
								<li>AC_Oil</li>
							</thingDefs>
						</value>
					</li>
					<li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
						<xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="VCE_DeepFrier"]/costList</xpath>
						<value>
							<costList>
								<Steel>40</Steel>
								<Chemfuel>20</Chemfuel>
							</costList>
						</value>
					</li>
				</operations>
			</li>
		</operations>
	</Operation>

</Patch>
